# pots v1.4 — WARN. Two contradictory pots:isStable values on one sample.
#
# THIS IS THE ONLY FIXTURE THAT CAN PROVE pots:PostureStabilityShape FIRES.
# The shape declares no sh:Violation constraint anywhere -- pots:isStable is
# sh:Warning, pots:stabilityScore and pots:atSeconds are sh:Info -- so an
# .INVALID.ttl for this class is impossible and would fail with NO_VIOLATION,
# and a .VALID.ttl passes whether or not the shape exists. .WARN. states the
# actual claim: something noticed this record, at Warning severity, and nothing
# rejected it.
#
# WHY REPEATING THE PROPERTY, WHEN A MISSING ONE WOULD BE THE OBVIOUS CHOICE.
# pots:isStable carries sh:datatype xsd:boolean and sh:maxCount 1 -- and NO
# sh:minCount. So omitting it entirely reports nothing at all, and a fixture
# written that way would fail with NO_WARNING while looking exactly like a
# reasonable test. The two ways to reach the warning are a non-boolean value or
# more than one value, and this fixture uses the second.
#
# EXACTLY ONE CONSTRAINT FIRES:
#   pots:PostureStabilityShape / path pots:isStable / MaxCountConstraintComponent
#
# true AND false on one sample is not a contrived shape for a graph to take. It
# is what a read-modify-write cycle produces when the writer adds a corrected
# reading instead of replacing the original -- the defect
# jayostis/sdk-typescript#38 describes on the reading side. The record then says
# the posture was both stable and unstable, and a consumer picking either answer
# is guessing. Warning rather than Violation is the right severity for it: the
# sample is still readable and the rest of the check is unaffected, so rejecting
# the whole record would lose more than it protects.
#
# EVERYTHING ELSE MUST BE CLEAN, or the fixture proves nothing -- a warn fixture
# that also violates something is rejected outright and is not evidence about the
# warning. Here that is easy, since the shape has no Violation constraint to
# breach; the Info-severity stabilityScore (0-1) and atSeconds (non-negative) are
# both in range anyway, so nothing else is reported at any severity.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix pots: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/pots/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:b0750009-0000-4a00-8000-000000004020> a pots:PostureStability ;
    pots:isStable true ;
    pots:isStable false ;
    pots:stabilityScore "0.41"^^xsd:double ;
    pots:atSeconds "420"^^xsd:integer .
